<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9777"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You know that investigators are busy tracing his timeline but it&#39;s a long line to trace. How many murders did he commit?  <BR>Here he was working for ADT installing security systems from 1974-1989. The opportunities for entrance into unsuspecting peoples homes is endless. <BR>He was a census taker in 1989. A serial killer working as a census taker! Wow! <BR>How about the time before WSU that he spent at Kansas Wesleyan and Butler Community College?  <BR>Go back further to his Air Force days. Is this where he first killed? Any unexplained unsolved murders in Korea, Turkey, Greece and Okinawa, Japan as the young BTK made his world tour?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
