</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Back down to 10 again. Johno We&#39;re trying to post the unaccounted for victims alongside as much info on Denny as we can scrounge up to see which ones can &#39;possibly&#39; be linked to him. I&#39;m sure that the investigators are working the same angle, but we might not see that info for years. If they release it early, fine, we can steal it and be done. <BR> <BR>I am personally amazed at the amount of time he had invested in church, and zoning board and having to be at at least some city commission meetings. He was also drawing pay as compliance official at the same time he worked at ADT. <BR> <BR>When did he have time to BTK. Now tonight on Larry King and Aaron Brown the subject of accomplices came to the front and center. Hattaburg admitted that the previous investigatiors were actively pursuing the angle, Beattie said it was possible and of course Charlie Otero has been pushing the idea all along. <BR> <BR>Consider the cars in the Davis/Hedge cases The Davis car was only 1/2 mile out of town, but the Hedge car was way out there. Either way, too far for a murderer to be walking home. I havent checked the map for RR tracks near the abandonment site leading back to town &#40;which is a valid possibility&#41; but everytime my car broke down at night when I was a teen&#40;lots&#41;and I was walking, a sheriff would pick me up and give me a ride. Either dogs barked and someone saw me out a window or someone driving by with a radio would call me in. <BR> <BR>Crossing cultivated fields is possible, but difficult, pasture land/oil field in the dark more likely. Cultivated fields normally have a perimeter road to check crop. Any open pasture area will have paths made by deer and other critters.  <BR> <BR>Another possability is to drop off a motorcycle using a pickup and hide it in the bushes. <BR> <BR>There are still some issues to deal with on the case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
