<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9916"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting timeline. <BR> <BR>IIRC, the Otero, Bright, Vian, and Wegerle murders happened during the day. The Fox murder was at night, as was the Williams incident. <BR> <BR>If I&#39;ve got this right, it might be interesting to find out &#40;if it&#39;s at all possible to&#41; when Rader&#39;s family left the house on overnight trips without him. I am of course operating on the theory that his day job was cover for his daytime murders, and that any nighttime activities would have been difficult to carry out with his family at home.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
