<!--Post: 9942--><!--Time: 1109711240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9942"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 1:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok I believe this time line are working on is important for two reasons. One the reason we started it to trace Rader&#39;s life to link him to every place he has been and to all of his victims, Now number two, I was serious about someone helping him, and I was going to let the idea go for now till I saw Charlie O on Larry King, and he said the same thing I did,  <BR>He feels that there is no way Rader did all this without someone helping him along the way, and also that he feels The reason Rader murdered his family has nothing to do with the other murders, that It is strange that his father was in the Air Force the same time As Rader and feels is father knew Rader from before. So in this timeline we need to figure out, one it might have been possible for Rader to mail some of his letter out of state, but if we can prove that he was in Park City on a particular date and did not leave, then someone else did it for him What do you all think? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9942-->
<!--Post: 9947--><!--Time: 1109712175-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9947"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 1:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Charlie is looking too hard for the <b><i>why</i></b> in all of this. Honestly. <BR> <BR>When we go through something so traumatic, we have this all consuming need to know why. And it would be too simple of an answer for it to be random. While I think he may have stalked one of the members in Charlie&#39;s house, I do not think it was a grudge crime against his father. I also do not think he had an accomplice. There has been nothing at all to support the accomplice theory that I can see.  <BR> <BR>Charlie is going to finally come to terms with the answer that sometimes there just is not a plausable answer. &#40;that will make sense to people who have faced trauma&#41;.  <BR> <BR>I think that through out the trial, when WPD finally has to give up evidence we are all going to learn that his crimes were about control/fantasy/fetishes &#40;I think there are a few of those&#41; and just plain anger and madness. <BR> <BR>His father may have known Rader via the AF, Mrs. Otero may have known him via Coleman, Charlie may have known him via cub scouts. Somewhere along the line, DR started fantasizing about either Mrs, Otero or Josephine. My guess is Mrs. Otero. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9947-->
<!--Post: 9950--><!--Time: 1109712299-->
