</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 9:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you Verm, your link illustrates the point perfectly. The pittsburg link has come up in passing &#40;I can&#39;t remember if if was you who mentioned it&#41;and now it&#39;s fact. <BR> <BR>Anyone who is happy to let the BTK case just go because they have a suspect in custody is missing the point. This is not a treasure hunt. It is about understanding. Someone, somewhere on the site was starting a string for compiling &#34;lessons learned&#34; about the case and Embersage is spearheading the effort to account for Raders trail which may turn up God knows what &#40;yes Embersage I&#39;m going to help but I&#39;m still trying to read through a lot of stuff I skimmed through earlier&#41;. <BR> <BR>I am not going to apologize for theorizing about accomplices or other victims or coverups or martian involvement or anything else that pops up as long as I&#39;m not satisfied that it&#39;s done deal. <BR> <BR>I can look at Rader&#39;s mugshot and tell that he&#39;s quite capable of all the killing but he is not going to be the last serial killer in history.   <BR>20 years from now, someone who is researching a new serial killer may look at this website. What are they going to find? Everyone dropped everything and walked away when their theory or profile didn&#39;t pan out? Or are they going to find information. <BR> <BR>Actually I&#39;m not pissed at people who think its all in the can, but I really don&#39;t see why they are concerning themselves that some of us would like to finish what we started. Google serial killer if you&#39;re bored, there are plenty to go around. <BR> <BR>If someone does know where the &#34;lessons learned&#34; string is would you please post the location on this one.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
