<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10773"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 11:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I borrowed this from Essevi, some AF info <BR> <BR> <BR>Dennis L. Rader was born March 9, 1945.  <BR> <BR>Parents are William E. Rader and Dorothea M. Rader.  <BR> <BR>He has three brothers:  <BR>Paul, born in 1947, Bill, born in 1949, and Jeff born in 1955.  <BR> <BR>He grew up in Wichita and spent his entire life in the Wichita area.  <BR> <BR>He graduated from Heights High School in Wichita in 1963.  <BR> <BR>Joined the USAF on Aug. 17, 1966.  <BR>Served for 4 years with an extended stint in the South Pacific.  <BR>He was stationed at Kadean AFB Okinawa, Japan and Tachikawa Air Base in Japan.  <BR>He left active duty on Aug. 9th 1970 and went on reserve duty until Dec. 1972.  <BR>Dennis Rader earned one Badge while in the AF, a small arms expert marksman badge. Likely earned right after basic training.  <BR>His specialty: Outside cable and antenna technician.  <BR> <BR>He was married on May 22, 1971 to Paula Dietz, the daughter of Hugo Palmer Dietz and Eileen Howard . She was born May 5, 1948.  <BR> <BR>He lived in Park City, Kansas since 1971. His home address is 6220 Independence St.  <BR> <BR>He attended Butler County Community College in El Dorado and Kansas Wesleyan University in Salina, KS.  <BR> <BR>He worked as an assembler at Coleman Co. at the Heating &amp; Air conditioning plant, 37th St from June 1971 to July 1973.  <BR> <BR>He entered Wichita State University in the fall of 1973 and graduated in 1979 with a degree in administration of justice.  <BR> <BR>During college he worked in the meat department for Leeker&#39;s IGA in Park City.  <BR> <BR>He was an installations manager for ADT Security, 431 N. Washington St, from November 1974 to July 1989.  <BR> <BR>He has 2 children, a son, Brian Howard, born on July 27, 1975 and a daughter, Kerri Lynn, born on June 13, 1978. His daughter currently lives in Farmington, Michigan. His son is a member of the U.S. Navy.  <BR> <BR>On Paula&#39;s 37th birthday, Sedgwick County authorities found the body now thought to be BTK&#39;s eighth victim, Marine Hedge. The 53-year-old widow was abducted from her home, just a few doors from the Rader family on North Independence Street.  <BR> <BR>He worked for the U.S. Census Bureau in 1989 as a census field operations supervisor.  <BR> <BR>He was a Cub Scout and Boy Scout leader with Cub Scout Pack 491 and then with Boy Scout Troop 491 - as his son progressed through scouting.  <BR> <BR>His father, William E. Rader, died on Dec. 27, 1996.  <BR>Obituary: William E. &#34;Bill&#34; Rader,74, retired KG&amp;E Ripley Generating Station plant operator; died Friday, Dec. 27, 1996. Survivors: wife, Dorothea: sons, Dennis, Jeff, both of Wichita, Paul of Falun, Bill of Climax; brothers, Ted of Wichita, Don of Grove, OK, Wallace of Mitchell, IN; eight grandchildren.  <BR> <BR>He had served on the Sedgwick County Board of Zoning Appeals and the Animal Control Advisory Board &#40;April 1996 - June 1998&#41;.  <BR> <BR>His most recent job was as a Compliance Supervisor for Park City, Kansas since May 10, 1991. The Oct. 4, 2001 issue of The Ark Valley News reported that Rader received a 10 year service award presented by Mayor Bergquist. He earned $16.62 per hour.  <BR> <BR>His wife, works as a bookkeeper at Snacks, the Diamond Shamrock convenience store located at 61st Street North and Broadway. A co-worker described Paula as hard-working, loyal and trustworthy. She has been working at the store for 20 years, She sang in the church choir.  <BR> <BR>May 2004 the Raders went to Farmington, Michigan to visit their daughter, Kerri and her husband Darian.  <BR> <BR>He is a 30-year member of the Park City Christ Lutheran Church and <!--/Text--></td></tr>
